    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0599" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-03T10:00:00-05:00">March 3, 1932—10 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Your 294, March 2, 11 a.m. If and when any notification is received with
                    regard to establishment of new regime in Manchuria, <pb facs="0600" n="496"
                        xml:id="pg496"/> inform Department but take no additional action in absence
                    of Department’s further instructions.</p>
                <p>Instruct Mukden and Harbin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
